@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+[
+{ type: install
+  message: <<EOM
+The collector writes to ClickHouse (databases/clickhouse), which may
+run on another host, as may SigNoz (net-mgmt/signoz). ClickHouse needs
+a cluster named "cluster" and ZooKeeper, as upstream's installation
+guide describes:
+
+  https://signoz.io/docs/install/linux/
+
+Before the first start, and after each upgrade, create or upgrade the
+SigNoz schema in ClickHouse:
+
+  sysrc signoz_otel_collector_clickhouse_dsn="tcp://localhost:9000"
+  service signoz_otel_collector migrate
+
+The collector reads %%ETCDIR%%/config.yaml, whose exporters
+write to ClickHouse on localhost. By default SigNoz manages it over
+OpAMP, as set in %%ETCDIR%%/opamp.yaml, and the collector
+ingests nothing until SigNoz answers there. To run config.yaml as it
+stands, without SigNoz:
+
+  sysrc signoz_otel_collector_manager_config=""
+
+By default the collector listens on all interfaces for OTLP on ports
+4317 (gRPC) and 4318 (HTTP), Jaeger on 14250 and 14268, HTTP logs on
+8081 and 8082, and health checks on 13133.
+EOM
+}
+]
